      "summaries": {
        "en": "Spec-kit is a Python toolkit for spec-driven development, helping teams align on clear specifications before writing code. It provides templates and workflows to define, review, and iterate on specs collaboratively, reducing misunderstandings and rework. The key insight is treating specs as living documents that evolve with the project, not static requirements. Use it to kickstart new features by drafting a spec, getting team feedback, and then coding against a shared blueprint—ideal for AI-assisted development with Copilot or similar tools.",
        "zh": "Spec-kit 是一个用于规范驱动开发的 Python 工具包，帮助团队在编码前就规范达成一致。它提供模板与工作流，支持规范的协作定义、审查与迭代，减少误解和返工。核心理念是将规范视为随项目演进的活文档，而非静态需求。用户可起草新功能规范、收集团队反馈，再按共享蓝图编码，尤其适合与 Copilot 等AI工具结合。通过紧密衔接规范与开发，spec-kit 提升协作效率，确保目标统一，是实践规范驱动开发的实用起点。",
        "es": "Spec-kit is a Python toolkit for spec-driven development, helping teams align on clear specifications before writing code. It provides templates and workflows to define, review, and iterate on specs collaboratively, reducing misunderstandings and rework. The key insight is treating specs as living documents that evolve with the project, not static requirements. Use it to kickstart new features by drafting a spec, getting team feedback, and then coding against a shared blueprint—ideal for AI-assisted development with Copilot or similar tools.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "spec-kit stands out for ai, copilot, and development in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Spec-kit is a Python toolkit for spec-driven development, helping teams align on clear specifications before writing code. It provides templates and workflows to define, review, and iterate on specs collaboratively, reducing misunderstandings and rework. The key insight is treating specs as living documents that evolve with the project, not static requirements. Use it to kickstart new features by drafting a spec, getting team feedback, and then coding against a shared blueprint—ideal for AI-assisted development with Copilot or similar tools.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/github/spec-kit for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
